  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Aaron reported this.  When running a SQL rebuild, the NSDL team noticed that the lowlevel storage file registry  writes the paths differently than Fedora normally does: it uses the \"canonical\" path (this is the path with any symlinks resolved).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The desired behavior is to save the path in the way it is configured in fedora.fcfg.  That way, the symlink target is respected later, if it changes.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "To recreate this problem:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "install an empty fedora repository.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "configure the objectPaths directory in fedora.fcfg to point to a symlink instead of a physical directory.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "create an empty object",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "note the associated path value in the objectPaths table (it will include the symlink as part of the path name)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "shut down fedora and do a sql rebuild",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "note the new path value in the objectPaths table (it will NOT include the symlink...instead it will contain the canonical path, which is not the desired behavior)",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    }
   ],
