  "description": "<p>Aaron reported this.  When running a SQL rebuild, the NSDL team noticed that the lowlevel storage file registry  writes the paths differently than Fedora normally does: it uses the \"canonical\" path (this is the path with any symlinks resolved).</p>\n\n<p>The desired behavior is to save the path in the way it is configured in fedora.fcfg.  That way, the symlink target is respected later, if it changes.</p>\n\n<p>To recreate this problem:</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>install an empty fedora repository.</li>\n\t<li>configure the objectPaths directory in fedora.fcfg to point to a symlink instead of a physical directory.</li>\n\t<li>create an empty object</li>\n\t<li>note the associated path value in the objectPaths table (it will include the symlink as part of the path name)</li>\n\t<li>shut down fedora and do a sql rebuild</li>\n\t<li>note the new path value in the objectPaths table (it will NOT include the symlink...instead it will contain the canonical path, which is not the desired behavior)</li>\n</ul>\n",
